'''''Dianthus callizonus''''', the '''beauty's girdle''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Caryophyllaceae]], endemic to the [[Piatra Craiului Mountains]] of Romania.<ref name="POWO_153178-1" >{{cite POWO |id=153178-1 |title=''Dianthus callizonus'' Schott & Kotschy |access-date=24 August 2022 }}</ref><ref name="RHS_5703" >{{cite web |title=''Dianthus callizonus'' beauty's girdle |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/5703/dianthus-callizonus/details |date=2022 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=24 August 2022 }}</ref> '''Garofița Pietrei Craiului''', the ''little carnation of Piatra Craiului'', as it is known in Romanian, is a symbol of the Piatra Craiului massif and the [[Piatra Craiului National Park|national park of the same name]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.pcrai.ro/lang-en/6/Park/flora-14.html |title=Piatra Craiului – Flora |author=<!--Not stated--> |date= |website=pcrai.ro |publisher=Parcul National Piatra Craiului |access-date=24 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120824175930/http://www.pcrai.ro/lang-en/6/Park/flora-14.html |archive-date=24 August 2012 }}</ref>
